M4.22 local artifact-hash query diagnosis
Date: 2026-08-28

Error image
-----------
One read-only local SHA-256 invocation referenced the nonexistent filename
`tu1nz_adult_commercial-host-access-gate.py`.

Cause
-----
The command used a hyphen where the versioned filename uses an underscore.
The failing lookup was suppressed for inventory continuity. The immediately
following literal-path query used the correct file and returned the expected
digest.

Risk
----
None to GitHub, the server or any runtime. The failed lookup returned no hash
and is not credited as evidence.

Rollback
--------
No rollback is required because the operation was read-only. This diagnosis
can be reverted with the M4.22 branch.

Approved continuation
---------------------
Use only the successful literal-path digest set in M4.22 evidence and keep the
typo diagnosis versioned.
